{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nCH=\\\"654a1fcfa363488db9f0459d74be6e99-question-0\\\"\nKQ=\\\"8dd4ec3c466747dc9a00545e17321baf-knowledge-0\\\"\nKINFL=\\\"fa5a6edbbfe243c7a66eb9f3eed7433b-knowledge-1\\\"\nfact={\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@leader_sync_accepted_identity\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a candidate that syncs from the greatest promise, the accepted index it ends with is the adopted promise's own accepted count whenever the resume point lies inside that promise's content: sync_idx is the candidate's decided or accepted index, the suffix is the adopted promise's log from there, and the carried StopSign adds the same one index the adopted promise already counted, so the two accounting terms cancel. Whenever the resume point lies beyond that content the suffix is empty and the candidate ends at sync_idx plus the StopSign term. A disagreement between the adopted decided index and the entries held therefore needs some promise reporting a decided index above the adopted promise's content.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Follows from the two branches of the follower's Promise (common_prefix = prep.decided_idx when na > prep.n_accepted, prep.accepted_idx when equal and greater) and sync_log's accepted accounting; the adopted promise is the strictly greatest under (n_accepted, accepted_idx). Sourced; the three-node runs of this investigation had the greatest promise also reporting the greatest decided index, so the disagreement never arose there.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"handle_majority_promises\\\",\\\"leader_state_promise_meta\\\",\\\"leader_state_max_decided\\\",\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"follower_promise_reports_accepted_idx\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{}}\ninterp={\\\"investigation_id\\\":CH,\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"handle_majority_promises\\\",\\\"leader_state_promise_meta\\\",\\\"leader_state_max_decided\\\",\\\"sync_log_accounting\\\",\\\"create_log_sync\\\",\\\"send_accsync_valid_entries\\\",\\\"follower_promise_reports_accepted_idx\\\",\\\"no_stopsign_decided_idx\\\"],\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"refuted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Refuted as an independent defect by source arithmetic, with the residual dependence stated. The candidate's accepted index after the prepare phase is determined by the adopted promise: with the resume point inside that promise's content the candidate ends at exactly the adopted promise's accepted count, because the suffix supplies the entries from the resume point to that content and the carried StopSign adds the same one index the adopted promise had already counted (the follower's Promise sets common_prefix to the candidate's decided index when its accepted round is higher, and to the candidate's accepted index when the rounds are equal and it is further ahead); with the resume point beyond that content the suffix is empty and the candidate ends at the resume point plus the StopSign term. In both cases the candidate's accepted index is at least the adopted promise's content, so for the adopted decided index to exceed the entries held some promise must report a decided index above the adopted promise's content. For truthful reports that is excluded by the protocol's own invariant that a promise with a higher accepted round covers everything decided - the property this code relies on instead of a local clamp - and for corrupted reports the only producers observed in this investigation are the inflated accepted indexes already covered by the parent question, which also leave the adopted decided index equal to or below the leader's accepted index in the newterm and staleleader stages. The two orderings coincided in every observed run, and no run produced a decided index above the adopted log's content, so the suspicion is refuted in its independent form while the residual case (a legal history in which the greatest-accepted promise is not the greatest decided reporter and the invariant fails) remains only as a consequence of the parent's corruption.\\\"),\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"No observed run produced a decided index above the adopted log's content, so the refutation rests on the source arithmetic plus the protocol invariant rather than on an executed witness.\\\",\n  \\\"The arithmetic uses the follower's two Promise branches; other sync producers (send_accsync) were not part of this pairing.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"The protocol invariant that a higher-round promise covers all decided entries is used as a premise, not proved here; the refutation stands only as long as it holds.\\\",\n  \\\"Only three-node clusters with at most a few terms and stopsign-carrying logs were exercised; a history that violates the invariant would need the corrupted reports of the parent question.\\\",\n  \\\"No execution was run for this account.\\\"],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":KQ,\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the leader adopts the log and the decided index from two independently ordered inputs\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"@leader_sync_accepted_identity\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the candidate's post-sync accepted index equals the adopted promise's accepted count when the resume point is inside its content\\\"},{\\\"entry_id\\\":KINFL,\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the inflated accepted index only arises from a resume point covering a carried StopSign\\\"}]}\nup={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Settle the child question by source arithmetic instead of chasing a variant of the parent's cause. The candidate's accepted index after the prepare phase equals the adopted promise's accepted count whenever the resume point lies inside that promise's content (the suffix supplies the remaining entries and the carried StopSign's +1 cancels against the one the adopted promise already counted), and equals the resume point plus that term otherwise; a disagreement between the adopted decided index and the entries held therefore requires a promise reporting a decided index above the adopted promise's content, which truthful reports cannot do under the invariant that a higher-round promise covers everything decided, and which the observed corrupted reports did not do either. The child interpretation is therefore explained/refuted in its independent form, a fact records the accepted-index identity and the required condition, and the question's residual is limited to histories that would also break the parent's invariant.\\\"),\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":CH,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n  \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"A legal history in which the greatest-accepted promise does not cover another promise's reported decided index would reopen this; the decisive observation would be a newly elected leader whose adopted decided index exceeds the entries its adopted log provides, with every promise's report consistent with its own content.\\\"}],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[fact],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(up, open('update.json','w'), indent=1); print('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 900\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
