{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Settled the child question by source arithmetic rather than by chasing a variant of the parent's cause. For a candidate that syncs from the greatest promise, the accepted index it ends with equals the adopted promise's own accepted count whenever the resume point lies inside that promise's content — the suffix supplies the remaining entries and the carried StopSign's +1 cancels against the one the adopted promise already counted — and equals the resume point plus that term otherwise; the follower's two Promise branches (common_prefix = the candidate's decided index when its round is higher, the candidate's accepted index when the rounds are equal and it is further ahead) determine which case applies, so the candidate's accepted index is always at least the adopted promise's content. A disagreement between the adopted decided index and the entries held therefore requires some promise reporting a decided index above the adopted promise's content: truthful reports cannot do that under the invariant that a higher-round promise covers everything decided (the property this code relies on instead of a local clamp), and the corrupted reports observed here produced no such witness either — the pairs of orderings coincided in every run, and the newterm/staleleader stages left the adopted decided index at or below the leader's accepted index. The child interpretation is therefore explained with defect_claim refuted in its independent form, a fact records the accepted-index identity plus the condition a disagreement would need, and the question is dispositioned explained with a residual discriminator naming the only reopening case (a legal history where the greatest-accepted promise does not cover another promise's reported decided index, which would also break the parent's invariant). The updates carry the premises honestly: the invariant is used, not proved, the arithmetic covers the Promise branches only, and no execution was run for this account. No execution was requested this turn; the parent question stays active with its five-receipt violated/asserted account, and the remaining incomplete items are loss- and timer-triggered re-synchronization, larger clusters, persistence across restarts, compaction calls, and any further independent lead.\"}"}}
